    "https://www.kwu.edu/about/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Kansas Wesleyan - Kansas Wesleyan University Skip to content Menu Open Search Search Web Site: About Overview News Events Faculty & Staff Directory Our Campus Our History and Traditions Our Mission and Values Discover Salina Strategic Plan Event Tickets Employment Opportunities Student Outcomes Data Consumer Information At Kansas Wesleyan, we are student-centered and community focused. About KWU Academics Overview Degrees and Programs Academic Departments Online Learning Dual Degree Programs Community Resilience Hub Student Complaint Procedures Student Support Resources Memorial Library Bookstore Registrar Scholarship Gala Careers at Kansas Wesleyan Overview Admissions Overview Admissions Events Undergraduates Graduate Students Transfer Students Student Health Insurance International Students Admissions Overview Pay for College Overview Tuition and Costs Net Price Calculator Payment Plans Financial Aid Scholarships Veteran and Military Benefits Pay for College Overview Student Life Overview Clubs and Organizations Campus Ministry Belonging and Inclusion Housing Athletics Fine Arts Events Navigate Career Services Center Accessibility Services Student Life Overview Alumni Overview Get Involved With An Alumni Chapter! Alumni Association Alumni Award Nomination Request a Transcript Alumni Shop Contact Magazine KWU Auxiliary Update Your Contact Information Alumni Overview Links for Current Students Parents Alumni My KWU KWU Email Canvas Request Info Visit Apply Give Careers at Kansas Wesleyan Home About Careers at Kansas Wesleyan How to Apply for Current Openings Please scroll down to see a list of currently open positions, and review each job description for specific application requirements and instructions. We are thrilled that you are interested in employment at Kansas Wesleyan University, one of the fastest-growing universities in the Midwest! KWU’s enrollment is up more than 40% since 2019, and the university has unveiled more than $12 million in capital improvements since 2022. That includes a new Nursing Education Center, significant renovations and improvements to Music facilities and the campus’ first newly constructed student housing in 60 years. If you become a Coyote, you are joining the place to be, a university truly moving toward greatness. You’re also joining a city on the rise, Salina ! Our hometown has a population of about 50,000, a diversified economy and has garnered national attention for its quality of life and for being a great place to raise a family. KWU is proud to be a member of the Salina community! Many of our departments have very strong ties to organizations throughout the city , and Salina’s recent growth provides opportunities for students and employees to contribute throughout the region. The area also offers entertainment and dining options unlike any other city of its size in the region. The library, park system and schools provide wonderful opportunities for those raising a family, while the downtown area has recently completed a multi-million dollar renovation that provides boutique shopping and award-winning local dining options. A complete listing of open positions is available below. Note that employees may reach the Human Resources office with any concerns at 785-833-4303 or [email protected] . Benefits Kansas Wesleyan offers an excellent standard benefits package, including medical, dental, vision and retirement options, and long-term disability and life insurance for full-time employees. In addition, other benefits include: Generous retirement contribution to TIAA, no match required, after 90 days. SafeZone access, for safety and emergency response no matter where you are, for all students, faculty and staff. Five meals per week at Bieber Dining Hall (full-time employees only). An average of 17 paid holidays a year, with a generous personal time-off policy. Four-day workweek in the summer. Free single membership to the Salina Family YMCA (discount for families). Free MBA program for full-time employees (50 percent off for spouses). The welcoming and inclusive campus is committed to resilience and sustainability, and all are welcome to spend time with our campus mental health dog, Schuyler (pictured at top right). An annual holiday schedule is also available. Some of the above benefits may vary depending on the position, but applicants are invited to contact [email protected] for specific information. Relevant Links HR Links Employee Handbook Employee Handbook Policies Faculty Handbook About Kansas Wesleyan Salina Links General Salina Links Links for Families Entertainment and Fine Arts Food and Drink Shopping Current Job Openings IMPORTANT NOTE: Each applicant must also download, complete and save under your name the KWU Employment Application , a fillable PDF form. Include this with your required application materials as outlined in the job description. _______________________ Athletics: Athletic Trainer Athletics: Bus Driver ___________________________________________________ Faculty: Adjunct Nursing Clinical Position _____________________________________________________ Staff: Cashier (Part-Time) Staff: Custodial Staff Staff: Facilities Maintenance Technician ____________________________________________________ Internal Job Openings – Internal Candidates Only This is a listing of current internal job openings. External candidates are not eligible for these positions. __________________________________________________________________ Apply Apply Request Info Request Info Visit Visit Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram Contact Us Careers at Kansas Wesleyan Policies Website Accessibility Consumer Information Accreditation Astra Campus Reservations Yotee’s Campus Store 100 E. Claflin Avenue Salina, KS 67401 785-827-5541 Kansas Wesleyan University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all rights, privileges, programs and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and/or ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © 2026 Kansas Wesleyan University"
    },
